<script>
  import { Button, InlineTip } from "carbon-components-svelte";
  import Dashboard from "carbon-pictograms-svelte/lib/Dashboard.svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Place a tip beside the setting or view it explains. Give it a `title` and put
the text in the default slot. A tip with no `id` is dismissed for as long as
the component lives, so these examples return when the page reloads. Give a tip
an `id` to remember its dismissal (see [Remembering dismissals](#remembering-dismissals)).

<InlineTip title="Sync your settings">
  Keep your layout, filters and theme on every device you sign in to.
</InlineTip>

## InlineTip, Callout or InlineNotification

| Use | When |
| --- | --- |
| InlineTip | The text teaches something the user can do, and the user may want it gone for good. A dismissal is remembered. |
| [Callout](/components/Callout) | The text is true for as long as the page is open, such as a limit or a prerequisite. It can't be dismissed. |
| [InlineNotification](/components/InlineNotification) | The text reports the result of something the user just did, such as a failed save. It is announced, and closing it is not remembered. |

## Content

### Learn more link

Set `href` for a "Learn more" link. The title describes it, so a page of tips
does not hold a list of identical link names. Change the wording with
`learnMoreText`.

<InlineTip title="Filter by owner" href="#filters">
  Narrow the table to the rows one person owns.
</InlineTip>

### Actions

Use the `actions` slot for what the tip teaches the user to do, after the
"Learn more" link.

<InlineTip title="Sync your settings" href="#sync">
  Keep your layout, filters and theme on every device you sign in to.
  <Button slot="actions" kind="tertiary" size="small">Turn on sync</Button>
</InlineTip>

### Illustration

The `illustration` slot holds art beside the text. It is hidden from screen
readers, and a collapsed tip hides it. In forced colors every `svg` takes the
`ButtonText` fill, so draw outline art with a CSS `fill: none` rule, not the
`fill="none"` attribute, which the forced rule outranks.

<InlineTip title="Read a dashboard at a glance" href="#dashboards">
  Each tile shows one metric over the range you pick above the charts.
  <Dashboard slot="illustration" />
</InlineTip>

### Heading level

The title is a heading. Inside a [Section](/components/Heading) it sits one
level below the section's heading, and elsewhere it is an `h3`. Set
`headingLevel` to fit the page outline.

<InlineTip headingLevel={2} title="Keep a backup">
  Export your workspace before you delete a project.
</InlineTip>

## Collapsible

Set `collapsible` to let users collapse a tip to its title. The title becomes
the disclosure button, so its name stays the same in both states. On the title,
press <DocKbd label="Enter" /> or <DocKbd label="Space" /> to toggle it. Set
`collapsed` to start collapsed, or bind it. Reduced motion skips the animation.

<InlineTip collapsible title="Work faster with keyboard shortcuts">
  Open the shortcut list from anywhere on the page to see every key for the
  view you are on.
</InlineTip>

## Dismissing

Press the close button, named "Dismiss tip" followed by the title, to remove a
tip. Keyboard focus returns to the control it came from, so the page does not
lose your place. Call `preventDefault()` on `on:dismiss` to keep the tip, and
set `dismissible` to `false` to remove the button. Replace the label with
`dismissText`, a function that receives the title.

<InlineTip
  title="Cuenta de facturación"
  dismissText={(title) => `Cerrar el consejo: ${title}`}
>
  Cambie los datos de facturación desde la página de Facturación.
</InlineTip>

## Remembering dismissals

### Tip store

A tip with an `id` is remembered. By default it keeps the dismissed ids in
`localStorage`, and every tab and every store on the page that shares the key
follows. For a page with several tips, create one store with `createTipStore`
and share it with `setTipStore`, so tips do not each read the storage. A tip
dismissed in code, with `tips.dismiss(id)`, is remembered like one the user
closed; do it when the user does what the tip taught.

Create the store inside a component, not at module scope, so server-rendered
requests do not share one.

<FileSource src="/framed/InlineTip/InlineTipSettings" />

### Show tips again

`tips.reset()` forgets every dismissal, and `tips.reset(id)` forgets one. Put it
behind a control on the settings page. The store is a Svelte store, so
`$tips.dismissed` is a reactive `Set` of the dismissed ids.

<FileSource src="/framed/InlineTip/InlineTipShowAgain" />

### Server rendering

A server does not know what a visitor dismissed, and the store never reads its
storage while it renders, so the server and the first browser paint agree. Until
the page mounts, a tip follows the store's `pending` option:

| Setup | A new visitor | A returning visitor |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `pending: "hide"`, the default | The tips appear when the page hydrates and push the content below them down by their height. | Nothing: no flash, no shift. |
| `pending: "show"` | Nothing. | The tips show, then remove themselves when the page hydrates, and the content moves up. |
| `initial`, from a cookie | Nothing. | Nothing. |
| Rendered in the browser only | Nothing: the tips mount before the first paint. | Nothing. |

Use the default for tips most visitors dismiss. It never shows a tip someone
already closed, and a page rendered with JavaScript off shows none. Use
`pending: "show"` for a tip that most visitors leave open, so their page does
not grow after load. To remove both shifts, store the dismissals in a cookie
with `cookieTipStorage`, read it on the server with `parseTipCookie`, and pass
the ids as `initial`. The store is then `ready` from the first render.

```ts
// src/hooks.server.ts
import { parseTipCookie } from "carbon-components-svelte";

export function handle({ event, resolve }) {
  event.locals.dismissedTips = parseTipCookie(
    event.request.headers.get("cookie"),
  );
  return resolve(event);
}
```

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script>
  import {
    cookieTipStorage,
    createTipStore,
    setTipStore,
  } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  export let data;

  setTipStore(
    createTipStore({
      storage: cookieTipStorage(),
      initial: data.dismissedTips,
    }),
  );
</script>

<slot />
```

### Custom storage

Pass any object with `read()` and `write(ids)` as `storage` to keep the ids
somewhere else, such as the user's preferences on a server. Both may return a
promise. Until a read settles, tips follow `pending`, and a dismissal made in
that time is kept. Add `subscribe(callback)` to report changes made elsewhere.
A failed read or write calls `onError`; the dismissal still holds until the page
closes.

<FileSource src="/framed/InlineTip/InlineTipServerSynced" />

## Guidebanner

### Basic

Pass the tips as an array. A guidebanner shows one tip at a time with a
counter, and previous and next buttons that wrap from the last tip to the
first. The close button dismisses every tip in the set, and the store
remembers each tip's id, so a tip added later shows on its own. A guidebanner
with one tip left drops the counter and the buttons.

Screen readers hear the region as a carousel and the tip as "1 of 3". The tip
is announced when a button changes it, and not when the banner first appears.

Share the store with a "Show tips again" control, and listen for `on:change`
and `on:dismiss`.

<FileSource src="/framed/InlineTip/GuidebannerDashboard" />

## Guidance

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Give every tip that should stay dismissed a stable `id`. | The id is the tip's name in storage. Renaming it shows the tip again. |
| Dismiss a tip in code once the user does what it taught. | The tip has done its job, and the user does not have to close it. |
| Keep a tip to a sentence or two, with one link. | A tip sits in the flow, so a long one pushes the page down. |
| Offer "Show tips again" somewhere users can find it. | A closed tip is gone for good, including one closed by mistake. |
| Pass the cookie ids as `initial` when the page is server rendered. | The server then renders the right tips, and nothing moves on hydration. |
